1
00:02:28,615 --> 00:02:34,281
<b>THE CLOWN</b>

2
00:04:39,479 --> 00:04:40,776
It's hot!

3
00:04:59,365 --> 00:05:01,356
<i>You</i> should have a fan.

4
00:05:23,756 --> 00:05:25,383
<i>57 people.</i>

5
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:27,850
<i>Including Mayor Romualdo.</i>

6
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:32,324
His wife is called Nancy.
She's a hairdresser.

7
00:05:32,398 --> 00:05:34,559
- Romualdo, Nancy.
- Romualdo, Nancy.

8
00:05:34,634 --> 00:05:37,364
Romualdo's kind <i>of</i> blind.
He wears thick glasses.

9
00:05:37,437 --> 00:05:39,667
- The town's <i>wacko</i> is Pinga.
- Pinga!

10
00:05:39,739 --> 00:05:41,536
He's nuts, an old drunk!

11
00:05:41,607 --> 00:05:46,408
And the brothel has the best name!
"The Snake's Armpit".

12
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:48,606
- OK! What about my father?
- As usual.

13
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:50,649
Give us a magic trick!

14
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,843
Here's the ball. It's gone!

15
00:05:54,387 --> 00:05:55,854
<i>Look!</i> An elephant!

16
00:06:48,341 --> 00:06:50,366
Ladies and...

17
00:07:16,869 --> 00:07:20,236
Ladies and gentlemen!
The Circus Esperanza...

18
00:07:20,306 --> 00:07:24,675
is proud <i>to</i> present the
greatest act in Latin America...

19
00:07:24,744 --> 00:07:26,234
in Europe...

20
00:07:26,379 --> 00:07:28,347
and <i>also</i> in Santa Rita <i>of</i> Ibitipoca.

21
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:32,243
I must ask <i>for</i> those <i>who</i> are
faint <i>of</i> heart <i>to</i> leave now!

22
00:07:32,318 --> 00:07:34,786
<i>While performing the act</i>
<i>you're about to see...</i>

23
00:07:34,854 --> 00:07:37,846
the famous Hans Sdrausen,
<i>from</i> the USSR...

24
00:07:38,224 --> 00:07:41,284
lost his sight and fell in love
with the neighbor's parakeet!

25
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,225
Is he <i>or</i> is he <i>not</i> crazier than Pinga?

26
00:07:44,764 --> 00:07:47,255
I beg <i>for</i> a round <i>of</i> applause
<i>to</i> such a myth...

27
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:49,494
a man <i>who</i> wandered through deserts
without sleeping...

28
00:07:49,569 --> 00:07:51,503
climbed mountains without eating...

29
00:07:51,571 --> 00:07:53,505
and sailed the seas without lying.

30
00:07:53,573 --> 00:07:56,337
And <i>who</i> shall <i>now</i> perform
exclusively before your eyes!

31
00:07:56,409 --> 00:08:00,345
Please welcome the fabulous,
the spectacular, the sensational...

32
00:08:00,413 --> 00:08:02,404
Thoroughbred!

33
00:08:36,315 --> 00:08:37,543
- <i>How</i> are you?
- I'm fine.

34
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:41,383
I'm talking <i>to</i> that charming lady
next <i>to</i> you. <i>How</i> are you?

35
00:08:41,454 --> 00:08:43,786
- Fine.
- What's your name, charming lady?

36
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:46,484
- Nancy.
- Is that a name?

37
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:49,761
Don't tell me you're the wife
<i>of the greatest mayor...

38
00:08:49,829 --> 00:08:51,729
in South America and North Africa!

39
00:08:52,832 --> 00:08:56,233
Dear <i>Mayor Ronaldo...</i>

40
00:08:56,302 --> 00:08:58,770
It's Romualdo, <i>you</i> moron!

41
00:08:58,838 --> 00:09:00,863
Don't bother me
<i>or I'll teach you</i> a lesson!

42
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,339
- Oh, really?
- Yes!

43
00:09:02,408 --> 00:09:04,774
- Oh, really?
- Yes, yes, yes!

44
00:09:04,844 --> 00:09:07,404
<i>Look,</i> people!
He's teaching lessons <i>for</i> free!

45
00:09:08,648 --> 00:09:11,811
I <i>know</i> this should be difficult
<i>for</i> those afraid <i>of</i> roaches...

46
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:14,819
but I need a brave woman
<i>from</i> the audience!

47
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:17,412
I am brave!

48
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:19,720
The other day I had four men run!

49
00:09:19,792 --> 00:09:21,919
- Run away <i>from</i> you?
- <i>No,</i> run after me!

50
00:09:22,361 --> 00:09:23,658
<i>You</i> wretch!

51
00:09:23,863 --> 00:09:26,957
These are all your children,
<i>you</i> cuckold!

52
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:28,257
Where's my money?

53
00:09:28,334 --> 00:09:31,895
Security, take away
that mad fat woman...

54
00:09:31,971 --> 00:09:34,496
<i>who</i> I've never seen before!

55
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,735
But be careful with my children!

56
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:40,610
I need a very brave woman!

57
00:09:41,447 --> 00:09:43,312
Anyone?

58
00:09:44,383 --> 00:09:48,285
Then we must call
the only true brave lady...

59
00:09:48,354 --> 00:09:50,413
that has ever set a <i>foot</i>
here and there!

60
00:09:50,489 --> 00:09:52,684
- <i>No, no, no!</i>
- Yes, yes, yes!

61
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,623
- <i>No, no, no!</i>
- Yes, yes, yes!

62
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:58,591
- Are <i>you</i> calling?
- Exactly! Excuse me!

63
00:09:58,664 --> 00:10:00,598
<i>Hello, operator!</i>

64
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:02,961
<i>I wish to make a long distance call...</i>

65
00:10:03,235 --> 00:10:05,294
<i>to 666, half a dozen and six.</i>

66
00:10:05,504 --> 00:10:07,836
That number is busy, ma'am.

67
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:11,239
Please hold <i>on</i> a moment
while I put <i>you</i> through...

68
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:13,301
the police <i>station</i> line.

69
00:10:13,379 --> 00:10:14,937
I wish <i>to</i> speak with Lola!

70
00:10:16,449 --> 00:10:18,349
- What? Arrested?
- Arrested!

71
00:10:18,417 --> 00:10:19,611
But <i>how</i> come?

72
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:22,352
- Killed someone?
- Killed someone!

73
00:10:22,421 --> 00:10:23,945
Killed <i>who?</i> Mary Horse-Kick?

74
00:10:24,857 --> 00:10:26,620
- With a knife!
- With a knife!

75
00:10:27,927 --> 00:10:29,724
<i>Hello,</i> Lola!

76
00:10:31,664 --> 00:10:35,532
Could <i>you</i> help us in a <i>mission</i>
<i>of the greatest importance?

77
00:10:35,668 --> 00:10:37,727
<i>How</i> long will <i>you</i> take <i>to</i> get here?

78
00:12:01,954 --> 00:12:07,824
<i>The bravest woman of the Western,</i>
<i>Eastern, and Icy Indies!</i>

79
00:12:08,427 --> 00:12:10,224
Lola!

80
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:25,836
- We're Thoroughbred...
- And Mongrel!

81
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:28,839
The greatest clowns
in the third world!

82
00:12:29,515 --> 00:12:30,573
Goodbye!

83
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:33,379
<i>You</i> shouldn't say "goodbye"
<i>to</i> the audience, <i>fool!</i>

84
00:12:33,452 --> 00:12:35,420
<i>You</i> should say "I'll see you",
<i>or something!

85
00:12:35,654 --> 00:12:37,485
I'll see <i>you or</i> something!

86
00:12:37,656 --> 00:12:38,782
<i>Now</i> will <i>you</i> excuse me!

87
00:12:38,858 --> 00:12:41,918
I have an important meeting
at "The Snake's Armpit"!

88
00:12:55,875 --> 00:12:58,400
- Did <i>you</i> fix that permit thing?
- I'll handle that, father.

89
00:12:58,611 --> 00:13:01,375
Benjee, we should shake
things here a little bit.

90
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:04,507
- Yeah. A little makeover.
- People like foreign artists.

91
00:13:04,583 --> 00:13:07,245
We could dye our hair
<i>to</i> pretend we're Russian!

92
00:13:07,453 --> 00:13:09,421
- <i>Got</i> any cash <i>for</i> that?
- Let's talk about that later!

93
00:13:09,488 --> 00:13:11,183
Hey, Benjee! Help us out!

94
00:13:11,257 --> 00:13:13,657
<i>We're the only ones</i>
<i>working here. That's not right.</i>

95
00:13:14,426 --> 00:13:16,519
Benjee, have <i>you</i> seen the first-aid kit?

96
00:13:16,595 --> 00:13:17,823
- What's wrong?
- <i>Got</i> a headache.

97
00:13:18,230 --> 00:13:20,323
- Talk <i>to</i> Lady Zaira.
- Lady Zaira.

98
00:13:20,399 --> 00:13:22,833
There's <i>no</i> way I can
work with these shoes.

99
00:13:24,770 --> 00:13:26,670
- Mr. Waldemar Gomes?
- That's my father.

100
00:13:26,872 --> 00:13:29,363
- And <i>you</i> are?
- Benjamim Savala Gomes.

101
00:13:29,575 --> 00:13:30,564
Can I see some ID, please?

102
00:13:33,779 --> 00:13:35,713
I've only <i>got</i> my birth certificate.

103
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,548
I <i>also</i> need <i>to</i> see
the circus' permit, please.

104
00:13:40,786 --> 00:13:42,447
I haven't <i>got</i> it yet.

105
00:13:43,789 --> 00:13:46,485
- Can <i>you</i> get me some tickets?
- Sure.

106
00:13:46,792 --> 00:13:49,522
My uncle will love this!
He loves the circus!

107
00:14:05,411 --> 00:14:06,673
<i>Do you need anything?</i>

108
00:14:07,413 --> 00:14:09,847
<i>No, Lady Zaira. It's OK...</i>

109
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:21,426
I walk around with this certificate.
But what for?

110
00:14:29,001 --> 00:14:30,525
I'm always in a hurry.

111
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:37,873
I'll wait until things <i>cool</i> down
<i>to</i> take care <i>of</i> it all.

112
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:44,706
Hey, Benjee.
Could <i>you</i> get me a new bra?

113
00:14:44,783 --> 00:14:48,446
The strap broke and my <i>boobs</i>
popped out <i>on</i> the stage.

114
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:09,400
<i>You</i> need
a <i>good</i> night <i>of</i> sleep, Benjamim.

115
00:15:44,643 --> 00:15:45,610
<i>Hi.</i>

116
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:48,847
Hi.

117
00:15:49,515 --> 00:15:50,641
You're very funny.

118
00:15:50,883 --> 00:15:51,850
- Am I?
- Yeah.

119
00:15:52,851 --> 00:15:55,183
- What's your name?
- Benjamim.

120
00:15:55,354 --> 00:15:56,321
I'm Ana.

121
00:15:57,389 --> 00:15:59,448
- Nice <i>to</i> meet you.
- <i>You too.</i>

122
00:15:59,858 --> 00:16:01,849
I really liked your work.

123
00:16:03,495 --> 00:16:04,484
Thank you!

124
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:07,830
Are <i>you</i> guys going <i>to</i> Passos?

125
00:16:08,233 --> 00:16:10,599
Passos?
I think...

126
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:12,237
I don't know...

127
00:16:12,438 --> 00:16:14,531
<i>You</i> should <i>go!</i>
People there will love <i>you</i> guys!

128
00:16:15,574 --> 00:16:16,700
Thank you.

129
00:16:23,415 --> 00:16:25,383
What's the town's name again?

130
00:16:25,451 --> 00:16:26,440
Passos.

131
00:16:27,419 --> 00:16:29,353
- And your name is?
- It's Ana.

132
00:16:29,888 --> 00:16:31,378
I'm Benjamim.

133
00:16:36,261 --> 00:16:39,389
If <i>you</i> ever pass by,
I work at <i>Aldo Auto</i> Parts.

134
00:16:39,565 --> 00:16:41,499
- <i>Aldo Auto</i> Parts?
- Yeah!

135
00:16:43,369 --> 00:16:45,929
OK, then... Bye!

136
00:16:47,639 --> 00:16:48,697
Bye, Ana.

137
00:17:37,790 --> 00:17:40,657
Fabulous!
What a fabulous troupe!

138
00:17:41,493 --> 00:17:44,291
Our town is happy <i>for</i> welcoming
such a talented group.

139
00:17:44,496 --> 00:17:46,361
What's your name,
my charming friend?

140
00:17:46,565 --> 00:17:48,658
I'm running out <i>of</i> charm,
but my name's Benjamim.

141
00:17:50,302 --> 00:17:51,496
Oh, did <i>you</i> hear that?

142
00:17:52,704 --> 00:17:55,730
We'd like <i>you to</i> come over
and have lunch with us.

143
00:17:55,941 --> 00:17:57,272
All <i>of</i> us?

144
00:17:57,776 --> 00:17:58,834
- Of course.
- Of course.

145
00:17:59,845 --> 00:18:03,303
<i>You</i> mean all <i>of</i> us?

146
00:18:22,301 --> 00:18:26,397
Dear artists, this is my son,
my wife, my sister.

147
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:29,233
It's an immense <i>honor</i>
<i>to</i> offer <i>you</i> this humble meal.

148
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:31,238
I hope <i>you</i> all can relish it.

149
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:35,273
I <i>know</i> what "relish" means,
but I have <i>no</i> clue about "immense".

150
00:18:36,281 --> 00:18:38,715
A toast <i>to</i> the artists!

151
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:42,717
- <i>You</i> like <i>seafood?</i>
- Uh-uh.

152
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:47,258
Darling, I wanna eat fish and beef.

153
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:28,394
I tell him <i>or you</i> tell him?

154
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:31,631
- <i>You</i> tell him.
- <i>You</i> tell him.

155
00:19:32,571 --> 00:19:34,971
Benjee, are <i>you</i> going
<i>to</i> pay us today?

156
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:36,739
We must send <i>mom</i> some cash.

157
00:19:37,342 --> 00:19:40,277
I'll talk <i>to</i> my father later,
<i>so</i> he'll settle that.

158
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:44,213
- It wasn't bad. 55 people came.
- <i>No,</i> it was 57. I counted.

159
00:19:44,416 --> 00:19:46,350
But the <i>mayor</i> and his wife
didn't pay.

160
00:19:46,552 --> 00:19:48,349
They didn't? What a nerve!

161
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:51,421
What about that <i>food?</i>
Doesn't that count?

162
00:19:51,723 --> 00:19:54,385
Yeah, but they could've
collaborated <i>too.</i>

163
00:19:54,459 --> 00:19:55,687
Otherwise things get difficult!

164
00:19:56,395 --> 00:19:59,523
Stupendous musicians!
What are your names?

165
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:02,461
- He's John, I'm <i>Chico</i> Humbug!
- We're the Humbugging Brothers!

166
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,297
<i>Do you</i> play Ravel's "Bolero"?

167
00:20:04,503 --> 00:20:05,800
<i>No,</i> only the "Brothel's Bolero".

168
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:08,804
- What's <i>for</i> dessert?
- Egg pudding.

169
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,639
Life <i>on</i> the road is great, isn't it?

170
00:20:12,844 --> 00:20:14,971
Yes, it's <i>good to</i> be out there.

171
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:20,443
Out there we listen, we see,
we hear, we perceive, and we talk.

172
00:20:25,290 --> 00:20:27,383
You're a serious type when
you're off the ring.

173
00:20:29,294 --> 00:20:33,731
<i>You</i> know, Benjamim.
I think my <i>son</i> is an artist.

174
00:20:34,299 --> 00:20:35,561
One can feel those things.

175
00:20:36,535 --> 00:20:40,471
I'd be flattered if he could
be in the <i>show</i> tomorrow.

176
00:20:41,506 --> 00:20:44,964
Can I ask him <i>to</i> read
a poem he's written?

177
00:20:50,015 --> 00:20:53,314
My sweet mom,
<i>you</i> only bring me joy.

178
00:20:53,518 --> 00:20:56,749
She takes care <i>of</i> daddy
and he takes care <i>of</i> the town.

179
00:20:56,955 --> 00:20:59,822
Our family lives in happiness.

180
00:21:00,225 --> 00:21:03,319
Mommy gives me a kiss
and daddy shows me the <i>good</i> ways.

181
00:21:12,871 --> 00:21:15,339
- He's <i>got</i> talent, Benjamim.
- A true artist!

182
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,337
Yes, very <i>good</i> indeed.

183
00:21:23,015 --> 00:21:25,677
- Can <i>you</i> think that over?
- Sure.

184
00:21:27,719 --> 00:21:30,210
<i>You got</i> an old bra
that I can spare, ma'am?

185
00:21:30,722 --> 00:21:32,519
A big old spare bra?

186
00:21:46,338 --> 00:21:49,432
Mrs. Nancy, I heard you're
the best hairdresser in town.

187
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:52,769
Oh, come on. Maybe <i>you</i>
could come over <i>to</i> my parlor.

188
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:54,275
It'd be such an honor!

189
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:56,606
In fact
we can't <i>do</i> extravagant things.

190
00:21:56,815 --> 00:22:00,342
<i>You</i> can all come. I won't charge
<i>you</i> anything. That will be a gift.

191
00:22:00,552 --> 00:22:02,213
Thank <i>you so</i> much.

192
00:22:02,954 --> 00:22:08,324
At this age, we have <i>to</i> change
<i>our looks</i> every <i>now</i> and then.

193
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:10,785
May I come <i>too,</i> Mrs. Nancy?

194
00:22:10,996 --> 00:22:12,395
Of course!

195
00:22:13,598 --> 00:22:15,259
You're <i>so</i> generous.

196
00:22:17,436 --> 00:22:20,462
<i>So</i> you're going
<i>to</i> Mrs. Nancy's parlor?

197
00:22:21,506 --> 00:22:23,736
<i>You</i> may even <i>look good</i> after that.

198
00:24:09,681 --> 00:24:11,706
Is Benjamim all right, Mom?

199
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,942
Leave him alone, son.

200
00:24:57,929 --> 00:24:59,260
<i>Pay attention, Patrick.</i>

201
00:24:59,464 --> 00:25:02,490
When I'm about <i>to</i> stab that wretch,
I'll make a move like this.

202
00:25:02,701 --> 00:25:04,669
Then <i>you</i> just have <i>to</i> come and say:

203
00:25:04,870 --> 00:25:08,567
<i>"Stop</i> it!" Then I say:
<i>"Who</i> are you?"

204
00:25:08,940 --> 00:25:12,740
And <i>you</i> reply: "I'm the angel
<i>who</i> came <i>to stop</i> that tragedy!

205
00:25:13,245 --> 00:25:14,212
<i>Got</i> it?

206
00:25:14,412 --> 00:25:16,277
<i>You</i> must come in, <i>or</i> he'll kill me.

207
00:25:18,383 --> 00:25:21,443
Candies! <i>Who</i> wants candies?

208
00:25:23,321 --> 00:25:25,789
Smoothies! Smoothies!

209
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:33,461
- <i>Good</i> evening, Mr. Mayor.
- <i>Good</i> evening.

210
00:25:34,466 --> 00:25:36,366
That wing is <i>too</i> big. Move slowly.

211
00:25:36,568 --> 00:25:38,433
<i>You</i> memorized those lines, didn't you?

212
00:25:38,637 --> 00:25:41,504
I'm the angel <i>who</i> came
<i>to stop</i> this tragedy.

213
00:25:41,573 --> 00:25:42,767
<i>Very good!</i>

214
00:25:45,343 --> 00:25:47,675
Soulless woman,
<i>you</i> didn't waste time!

215
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:49,403
<i>You</i> left me <i>for</i> that bastard!

216
00:25:49,814 --> 00:25:50,803
I'm an honored man!

217
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:55,512
I'm <i>not</i> guilty <i>of</i> taking away
the only thing you've ever had!

218
00:25:58,356 --> 00:26:03,555
I'm doomed, a dishonored woman!
Murder me, I beg you!

219
00:26:03,728 --> 00:26:06,526
Shut up, woman,
<i>for</i> you're <i>not</i> worth anything!

220
00:26:07,265 --> 00:26:09,460
<i>You're the bastard</i>
<i>who ruined my life.</i>

221
00:26:09,768 --> 00:26:12,236
But <i>now you</i> shall get
what <i>you</i> deserve!

222
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:15,964
<i>Don't do that to a brother,</i>
<i>a God's son!</i>

223
00:26:16,341 --> 00:26:18,901
<i>Your fate is set, Devil's son!</i>

224
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:21,208
<i>Now</i> die like a man!

225
00:26:25,817 --> 00:26:26,784
<i>Go</i> on, boy!

226
00:26:26,985 --> 00:26:29,545
But he raised a knife.
Where's that wooden stick?

227
00:26:29,888 --> 00:26:31,515
The boy? Where's he?

228
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:33,558
The boy!

229
00:26:37,529 --> 00:26:38,655
<i>Who</i> are you?

230
00:26:39,464 --> 00:26:40,556
<i>Who</i> are you?

231
00:26:43,335 --> 00:26:44,427
<i>Who</i> are you?

232
00:26:44,703 --> 00:26:46,637
I'm the mayor's son, remember?

233
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,356
<i>Bravo!</i>

234
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:19,937
<i>Bravo!</i>

235
00:28:33,378 --> 00:28:34,367
Find the ball!

236
00:28:34,612 --> 00:28:36,375
- This one!
- Nope!

237
00:28:36,614 --> 00:28:37,706
Oh, dad!

238
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:39,315
- Where is it?
- Here!

239
00:28:39,517 --> 00:28:40,541
Nope!

240
00:28:42,454 --> 00:28:43,443
Where is it?

241
00:28:43,922 --> 00:28:44,946
<i>Here!</i>

242
00:28:45,323 --> 00:28:47,291
<i>Wrong again, my princess.</i>

243
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:03,467
You're the circus owner, ain't you?

244
00:29:03,942 --> 00:29:05,637
<i>No,</i> I can't take it at this time.

245
00:29:06,678 --> 00:29:09,340
Oh, come on! It is <i>good for</i>
washing down our organs.

246
00:29:13,952 --> 00:29:15,579
It's nice <i>to</i> be the owner, isn't it?

247
00:29:16,454 --> 00:29:17,546
Yeah.

248
00:29:17,622 --> 00:29:22,321
A while <i>ago,</i> I used <i>to</i> own
a textile factory with my father.

249
00:29:24,863 --> 00:29:26,694
We even sold fabrics <i>to São Paulo.</i>

250
00:29:28,399 --> 00:29:31,300
But then we started fighting.

251
00:29:31,369 --> 00:29:34,202
He convinced me <i>to</i> sell the business...

252
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:37,467
<i>to</i> invest in rice.

253
00:29:40,545 --> 00:29:42,240
But what did we <i>know</i> about rice?

254
00:29:43,414 --> 00:29:44,346
Nothing.

255
00:29:44,916 --> 00:29:46,406
We lost everything.

256
00:29:51,589 --> 00:29:52,886
But that's OK.

257
00:29:54,325 --> 00:29:56,418
I'm much better off now.

258
00:29:58,496 --> 00:30:03,433
Everyone should <i>do</i>
what they <i>do</i> best.

259
00:30:06,437 --> 00:30:07,529
Cats drink milk...

260
00:30:08,740 --> 00:30:10,298
mice eat cheese...

261
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:13,603
and I run my business.

262
00:30:17,549 --> 00:30:18,743
Excuse me.

263
00:30:55,820 --> 00:30:57,310
<i>Chico</i> and John.

264
00:30:58,356 --> 00:31:00,381
And here's a down payment...

265
00:31:00,892 --> 00:31:02,484
<i>for</i> the <i>two of</i> you!

266
00:31:03,995 --> 00:31:05,394
<i>You</i> tell him.

267
00:31:05,563 --> 00:31:08,862
If <i>you</i> could advance the whole pay,
it'd be nice.

268
00:31:09,267 --> 00:31:12,896
<i>You</i> know, our uncle is ill,
back in <i>Nepomuceno...</i>

269
00:31:13,304 --> 00:31:15,829
and we wanted
<i>to</i> send him some cash.

270
00:31:17,575 --> 00:31:19,668
Wasn't it your mother
<i>who</i> was in trouble?

271
00:31:21,946 --> 00:31:23,846
- She's well now.
- Thank you.

272
00:31:59,884 --> 00:32:02,614
Sweetheart, remember
the story <i>mom</i> told you?

273
00:32:03,888 --> 00:32:09,622
If <i>you</i> ever need anything,
pray <i>to</i> Saint Genesius.

274
00:32:11,663 --> 00:32:16,760
He's the <i>patron of</i> musicians,
comedians and clowns.

275
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:20,563
He protects Quarter Pounder...

276
00:32:21,706 --> 00:32:25,733
he protects Double-Jointed,
as well as Benjamim.

277
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:31,905
He protects us, sweetheart!

278
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:07,849
I think the engine's broken down.

279
00:33:08,386 --> 00:33:09,853
Let me see that.

280
00:33:17,428 --> 00:33:19,828
- The engine's broken down.
- I've already said that!

281
00:33:20,431 --> 00:33:21,659
Let's find help.

282
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:32,533
I had an awful dream, guys!

283
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:35,875
Can't get <i>to</i> sleep now!
I dreamed I was dating a goat!

284
00:33:35,947 --> 00:33:39,940
Then we bred and the offspring...
they looked like me!

285
00:34:06,944 --> 00:34:10,209
We <i>got</i> a problem with our truck.
Can <i>you</i> help us out?

286
00:34:12,850 --> 00:34:15,216
I think the <i>Parrot</i> Brothers
can help <i>you</i> out.

287
00:34:15,286 --> 00:34:16,776
Here's what <i>you</i> should <i>do.</i>

288
00:34:16,854 --> 00:34:19,618
<i>You go</i> straight.
<i>You go, go, go.</i>

289
00:34:19,690 --> 00:34:21,920
Then, turn right and <i>go, go, go.</i>

290
00:34:22,293 --> 00:34:26,286
Then <i>you go</i> across the plank,
then <i>go, go.</i>

291
00:34:26,364 --> 00:34:28,594
I <i>know</i> it's <i>not</i> easy <i>to</i> get it.

292
00:34:28,966 --> 00:34:32,424
Fortunately I have a map <i>to</i> sell you.
<i>Do you</i> want it?

293
00:34:37,341 --> 00:34:40,208
Hey, Benjamim, this map
says "Venezuela".

294
00:35:00,798 --> 00:35:02,789
<i>Good to</i> have folks around!

295
00:35:02,867 --> 00:35:04,801
- Seu Rob?
- <i>No,</i> I'm Bob.

296
00:35:04,869 --> 00:35:08,464
I guess you're looking <i>for</i> Rob.
<i>Are you looking for Bob or Rob?</i>

297
00:35:08,539 --> 00:35:10,200
We're looking <i>for</i> help.

298
00:35:10,274 --> 00:35:12,299
- Trouble with the police?
- <i>No.</i>

299
00:35:12,376 --> 00:35:13,604
Is this about drugs?

300
00:35:13,678 --> 00:35:17,637
<i>No!</i> It's our truck.
The engine's broken down.

301
00:35:17,748 --> 00:35:19,477
<i>Then you should talk to Rob.</i>

302
00:35:19,784 --> 00:35:21,308
But is <i>Rob</i> here?

303
00:35:21,385 --> 00:35:23,819
I don't know.
I haven't talked <i>to</i> him in 15 years.

304
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:31,894
- <i>Good</i> morning.
- <i>Good</i> morning! Are <i>you</i> Bob?

305
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,193
<i>No,</i> Rob.
Are <i>you</i> looking <i>for Bob or</i> Rob?

306
00:35:34,332 --> 00:35:37,324
<i>No!</i> Listen, our truck
has broken down.

307
00:35:37,401 --> 00:35:40,199
I see. And <i>you</i> bought
a map <i>of</i> Venezuela.

308
00:35:40,805 --> 00:35:43,899
- Could <i>you</i> help us out?
<i>- I can go there tomorrow.</i>

309
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:46,739
- Why tomorrow?
- I don't work <i>on</i> Saturdays.

310
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:50,178
Those are my principles,
but I have others.

311
00:35:50,248 --> 00:35:51,875
Are <i>you</i> talking about money?

312
00:35:51,949 --> 00:35:54,747
Mental agility is something I admire!

313
00:36:01,792 --> 00:36:05,455
Is there anymore?
Will the ladies find some?

314
00:36:16,841 --> 00:36:19,435
What about that little one?

315
00:36:34,892 --> 00:36:36,416
<i>Dubious origin!</i>

316
00:36:36,561 --> 00:36:39,655
Give it back <i>to</i> him.
Let's get down <i>to</i> work!

317
00:36:39,730 --> 00:36:43,427
When <i>you</i> come back, remind me
<i>of not</i> talking <i>to</i> you, <i>you</i> prick!

318
00:36:51,242 --> 00:36:53,437
<i>I love your mother</i>

319
00:36:55,279 --> 00:36:58,771
<i>She's the soul mate I dreamed of</i>

320
00:37:00,585 --> 00:37:03,315
<i>I love your mother</i>

321
00:37:04,589 --> 00:37:08,457
<i>For I married her one day</i>

322
00:37:30,982 --> 00:37:32,745
Did any <i>of you</i> touch this?

323
00:37:32,817 --> 00:37:34,751
My <i>son</i> tried <i>to</i> find the problem.

324
00:37:34,819 --> 00:37:36,684
- He's curious, ain't he?
- Yeah.

325
00:37:40,992 --> 00:37:42,516
Pump it up!

326
00:38:14,225 --> 00:38:16,557
People <i>of</i> Holy Jesus <i>of</i> Red River!

327
00:38:17,295 --> 00:38:19,354
Circus Esperanza has arrived...

328
00:38:19,430 --> 00:38:22,228
featuring the greatest
artists in Russia!

329
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:26,498
Dimitri Constantin
and Martina Dostoievska!

330
00:38:32,777 --> 00:38:35,974
- Is there guava today?
- Yes, sir!

331
00:38:36,247 --> 00:38:39,614
- Is there marmalade today?
- Yes, sir!

332
00:38:39,684 --> 00:38:43,518
- And the clown, what is he?
- He's a wives' thief!

333
00:39:20,958 --> 00:39:23,722
<i>Three, two, one, go!</i>

334
00:39:25,763 --> 00:39:27,924
<i>Hooked, hooked...</i>

335
00:39:43,247 --> 00:39:45,647
Benjee, I hope <i>you</i> don't mind...

336
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:49,277
but we're setting the tent
against the wind direction.

337
00:39:49,887 --> 00:39:52,321
You're right, Quarter Pounder. Thanks.

338
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:55,917
I'm sorry about that.
Let's set it up again.

339
00:40:16,914 --> 00:40:19,815
<i>- How much is that one?</i>
- 200.

340
00:40:22,319 --> 00:40:23,843
- And that smaller one?
- That's 100.

341
00:40:26,957 --> 00:40:28,185
- Can I pay in installments?
- Sure!

342
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:32,218
I'll need your ID, social security
and a fixed address.

343
00:40:33,664 --> 00:40:36,326
Can it be just my birthday certificate?

344
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:39,700
- Why didn't <i>you</i> buy it?
- <i>Too</i> expensive.

345
00:40:41,672 --> 00:40:42,866
Hey, Benjee.

346
00:40:44,675 --> 00:40:46,404
<i>Do you</i> like me?

347
00:40:51,515 --> 00:40:55,508
<i>Chico</i> Humbug said that I stink.

348
00:40:56,353 --> 00:40:57,718
<i>Do</i> I stink?

349
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:32,883
I'm the one selling candies now!

350
00:41:34,558 --> 00:41:35,786
It's quite difficult.

351
00:41:35,860 --> 00:41:37,589
<i>Good</i> luck, my friend!

352
00:41:41,999 --> 00:41:45,662
<i>Look.</i> That aches. That's better.

353
00:41:50,574 --> 00:41:53,338
I don't <i>know</i> what that is.
I've been <i>to</i> many doctors.

354
00:41:53,410 --> 00:41:54,900
None could find out what I have.

355
00:41:54,979 --> 00:41:57,504
That's high pressure
and a <i>low</i> Willy.

356
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:01,950
Hey, is it normal <i>to</i> dream <i>of</i> goats?

357
00:42:02,219 --> 00:42:03,413
Shut up!

358
00:42:05,689 --> 00:42:09,420
Aren't <i>you</i> embarrassed
<i>of walking around with that hair style?

359
00:42:09,560 --> 00:42:11,721
Your <i>mom</i> liked it, <i>you</i> prick.

360
00:42:12,897 --> 00:42:14,660
What about your wife?

361
00:42:14,732 --> 00:42:16,700
<i>You</i> bet she did!

362
00:42:18,235 --> 00:42:19,896
<i>Now you</i> ask me.

363
00:42:36,787 --> 00:42:39,620
That canvas won't last
<i>for</i> another year.

364
00:42:58,809 --> 00:43:00,709
When we get there...

365
00:43:01,979 --> 00:43:03,708
I'll pawn this accordion.

366
00:43:12,990 --> 00:43:14,389
Father...

367
00:43:18,362 --> 00:43:20,296
I think I can't take it anymore...

368
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:22,596
What is it, son?

369
00:43:25,569 --> 00:43:27,628
- Are <i>you</i> cold?
- Very much.

370
00:43:27,705 --> 00:43:31,436
Oh, come here,
I'll warm <i>you</i> up, sweetheart.

371
00:43:31,508 --> 00:43:33,476
<i>- Really?</i>
<i>- Really.</i>

372
00:43:36,714 --> 00:43:37,840
<i>No</i> accordion.

373
00:43:40,684 --> 00:43:42,208
Take it off!

374
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:22,954
WELCOME TO
MONTES CLAROS

375
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:37,235
Aren't we going <i>to</i> bury the dead?

376
00:44:38,375 --> 00:44:40,570
We don't <i>know</i> this soil.

377
00:44:41,512 --> 00:44:43,347
I thought we didn't have <i>to.</i>

378
00:44:43,347 --> 00:44:44,837
Where've <i>you got</i> your head at?

379
00:44:45,649 --> 00:44:47,514
<i>Stop it! Stop it!</i>

380
00:44:47,818 --> 00:44:49,649
<i>Put it down! Down!</i>

381
00:44:51,488 --> 00:44:54,719
<i>Let's put that tent down!</i>
<i>Come on! Come on!</i>

382
00:44:54,858 --> 00:44:58,316
<i>Down! Down with the canvas!</i>

383
00:44:58,395 --> 00:44:59,726
<i>Let's go!</i>

384
00:45:00,397 --> 00:45:02,262
<i>Come on!</i>

385
00:45:02,466 --> 00:45:04,297
I don't want <i>to</i> see it like that!

386
00:45:05,235 --> 00:45:07,533
If the wind blows, it's coming down!

387
00:45:20,684 --> 00:45:22,675
Isn't Benjamim coming in?

388
00:45:22,753 --> 00:45:24,380
I'll talk <i>to</i> him.

389
00:45:24,455 --> 00:45:26,787
Leave him alone, guys.

390
00:45:36,700 --> 00:45:40,363
Have <i>you</i> ever had the chance
<i>of meeting a foreign artist?

391
00:45:41,472 --> 00:45:42,666
<i>No.</i>

392
00:45:42,873 --> 00:45:45,706
Dimitri Constantin. <i>Yo soy</i> Russian.

393
00:45:45,909 --> 00:45:49,572
<i>You</i> aren't Russian here <i>or</i> in China.
Where are <i>you</i> from?

394
00:45:49,646 --> 00:45:51,637
<i>Maceio,</i> Jatiuca...

395
00:45:54,618 --> 00:45:56,518
- <i>You</i> married?
- Yes.

396
00:45:57,621 --> 00:45:59,646
- Are <i>you</i> afraid?
- Very much.

397
00:45:59,957 --> 00:46:01,652
But I take chances.

398
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:04,552
I'll be off <i>soon.</i>

399
00:46:04,628 --> 00:46:06,289
I'll be waiting.

400
00:46:27,851 --> 00:46:29,443
You're <i>from</i> the circus, uh?

401
00:46:29,520 --> 00:46:31,784
- <i>How do you</i> know?
- Because <i>of</i> your sissy style.

402
00:46:33,557 --> 00:46:35,650
Don't <i>you</i> have
women in your troupe?

403
00:46:35,726 --> 00:46:36,818
Yes.

404
00:46:36,894 --> 00:46:39,624
<i>So</i> quit messing around
with other people's women.

405
00:46:52,576 --> 00:46:55,477
<i>Do you</i> have a bra <i>to</i> spare?

406
00:46:57,614 --> 00:46:59,775
- <i>For</i> you?
- Yes.

407
00:47:01,718 --> 00:47:03,276
I mean, <i>no.</i>

408
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:07,713
It's <i>for</i> someone else.

409
00:47:09,993 --> 00:47:11,460
Oh.

410
00:47:15,532 --> 00:47:17,830
I'll never bury the dead
by myself again.

411
00:47:18,268 --> 00:47:22,261
By yourself?
We did it together, <i>Chico.</i>

412
00:47:22,339 --> 00:47:25,672
I might have <i>not</i> dug it,
but I helped cover it with sand.

413
00:47:31,582 --> 00:47:33,573
Is <i>Passos too</i> far <i>from</i> here?

414
00:47:33,650 --> 00:47:34,912
<i>Not</i> really.

415
00:47:35,752 --> 00:47:37,481
It's a <i>two-</i> day journey.

416
00:47:51,602 --> 00:47:53,331
I'm tired.

417
00:47:55,372 --> 00:47:56,669
Of what?

418
00:47:58,475 --> 00:47:59,840
Of everything!

419
00:48:01,545 --> 00:48:03,570
Tired <i>of</i> doing what I <i>do.</i>

420
00:48:05,582 --> 00:48:08,642
- What <i>do you do?</i>
- I work at a circus.

421
00:48:09,987 --> 00:48:11,784
- As a tamer?
- <i>No.</i>

422
00:48:12,356 --> 00:48:14,722
- Globe <i>of</i> Death?
- <i>No, no.</i>

423
00:48:16,927 --> 00:48:18,485
As a clown.

424
00:48:28,238 --> 00:48:29,899
I make people laugh...

425
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:34,707
but <i>who</i> in this world
will make me laugh?

426
00:48:42,686 --> 00:48:44,313
<i>I need to...</i>

427
00:48:46,556 --> 00:48:48,319
<i>get some sleep. I need...</i>

428
00:48:49,593 --> 00:48:52,653
<i>to</i> fix that ID thing, I need <i>to...</i>

429
00:48:53,697 --> 00:48:55,790
buy new boots, a new bra.

430
00:48:55,866 --> 00:48:58,767
It's about time
we replace the candies.

431
00:49:02,539 --> 00:49:04,336
You're funny.

432
00:49:35,339 --> 00:49:36,931
<i>Do you</i> have a fan?

433
00:49:42,679 --> 00:49:45,739
Emergency?
Send a <i>patrol</i> over right away!

434
00:49:52,289 --> 00:49:55,656
<i>Today is my wife's birthday, Cleide.</i>

435
00:49:55,926 --> 00:49:59,191
<i>People are having some</i>
<i>cheese and wine at my place.</i>

436
00:49:59,796 --> 00:50:03,562
I don't need <i>to</i> tell <i>you how</i> upset
I am <i>for not</i> being there.

437
00:50:04,634 --> 00:50:07,728
<i>Not</i> really <i>for</i> the wines,
but <i>for</i> the cheese.

438
00:50:08,372 --> 00:50:10,203
I like cheese very much.

439
00:50:11,541 --> 00:50:13,873
<i>My cat... Lincoln...</i>

440
00:50:15,545 --> 00:50:18,412
is suffering <i>from</i> terrible fur loss.

441
00:50:20,650 --> 00:50:22,675
<i>You</i> probably don't <i>know</i> anything...

442
00:50:22,753 --> 00:50:26,587
about wine, cheese,
and much less, cats.

443
00:50:27,691 --> 00:50:30,421
There are <i>two</i> kinds <i>of</i> fur loss:

444
00:50:31,728 --> 00:50:34,891
The periodical shedding...

445
00:50:36,233 --> 00:50:39,259
and the bad one...

446
00:50:40,771 --> 00:50:42,830
caused by allergy <i>to</i> mange.

447
00:50:43,640 --> 00:50:48,839
My aunt Valkyrie,
the pharmacy owner, had mange.

448
00:50:50,580 --> 00:50:52,172
And my cat...

449
00:50:54,217 --> 00:50:55,775
caught it <i>from</i> her.

450
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:59,655
The problem is that the cat
licks himself all the time...

451
00:50:59,723 --> 00:51:03,284
and ended up with a
fur ball in his stomach...

452
00:51:03,794 --> 00:51:06,627
which could only be
removed surgically.

453
00:51:08,832 --> 00:51:10,697
And that's what happened today.

454
00:51:11,501 --> 00:51:14,868
He was operated and went fine.
He's home now.

455
00:51:16,440 --> 00:51:19,876
I don't need <i>to</i> say
<i>how</i> upset I am <i>not to</i> be there.

456
00:51:20,811 --> 00:51:22,938
<i>Not</i> really <i>for</i> my wife, but...

457
00:51:23,847 --> 00:51:25,508
<i>for</i> Lincoln.

458
00:51:26,249 --> 00:51:27,739
The <i>question</i> is:

459
00:51:27,818 --> 00:51:30,446
What's with that burying thing?

460
00:51:30,787 --> 00:51:33,779
It's <i>not</i> a dead body, sir.
It's circus slang.

461
00:51:33,857 --> 00:51:35,688
We call it <i>"to</i> bury the dead".

462
00:51:35,759 --> 00:51:40,458
That's it.
When we find sandy soil...

463
00:51:40,530 --> 00:51:44,330
we need <i>to</i> put the weights
that hold the pole.

464
00:51:44,434 --> 00:51:46,629
And we call those weights the dead.

465
00:51:46,703 --> 00:51:47,829
Right!

466
00:51:47,904 --> 00:51:53,638
What about the time <i>you</i> deprived
me <i>from</i> Lincoln's company?

467
00:52:05,422 --> 00:52:07,287
Shut that <i>door.</i>

468
00:52:46,329 --> 00:52:50,527
Have <i>you</i> heard <i>of Aldo Auto</i> Parts?

469
00:52:52,602 --> 00:52:53,830
<i>What time is it?</i>

470
00:52:56,940 --> 00:52:58,874
<i>What time is the show this evening?</i>

471
00:52:58,942 --> 00:53:00,341
<i>At 11.</i>

472
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:00,760
<i>33 people.</i>

473
00:54:00,937 --> 00:54:03,701
The <i>mayor</i> is called Silas.
<i>Got</i> it? Silas!

474
00:54:03,773 --> 00:54:07,869
<i>His wife is called Quiteria.</i>
<i>The local wacko is Geronimo.</i>

475
00:54:07,944 --> 00:54:10,640
<i>He's into riding around barefoot.</i>

476
00:54:10,780 --> 00:54:14,876
<i>The mayor is Silas.</i>
<i>The wacko, Geronimo!</i>

477
00:54:14,951 --> 00:54:16,509
How's my father?

478
00:54:16,953 --> 00:54:18,352
As usual.

479
00:54:48,685 --> 00:54:52,451
<i>Mayor</i> Geronimo!

480
00:54:55,725 --> 00:54:58,216
<i>Mayor</i> Geronimo!

481
00:54:58,695 --> 00:54:59,923
Candies!

482
00:55:01,431 --> 00:55:02,921
<i>Who</i> wants candies?

483
00:55:03,600 --> 00:55:06,797
Candies <i>for</i> free!

484
00:55:11,841 --> 00:55:17,802
<i>Tip, tip, tip, ton</i>
<i>Tip, tip, tip, ton</i>

485
00:55:17,881 --> 00:55:23,217
<i>I sing like this</i>
<i>to ease your broken heart</i>

486
00:55:25,488 --> 00:55:27,547
<i>Tip, tip, tip, ton</i>

487
00:55:27,624 --> 00:55:34,655
<i>I sing like this</i>
<i>to ease your broken heart</i>

488
00:55:40,737 --> 00:55:43,638
<i>Mayor</i> Geronimo!

489
00:55:44,741 --> 00:55:47,710
Beautiful Mrs. Quiteria!

490
00:56:05,495 --> 00:56:07,656
Those <i>who</i> drink <i>too</i> much in Easter...

491
00:56:07,731 --> 00:56:09,494
don't make it <i>to</i> Christmas.

492
00:56:09,566 --> 00:56:11,693
<i>Booze</i> can be lethal!

493
00:56:11,768 --> 00:56:14,464
I think I'll move <i>into</i> a hospital!

494
00:56:14,537 --> 00:56:17,233
That was Mongrel, the clown...

495
00:56:17,307 --> 00:56:22,335
with his newest act
"The Misdeeds <i>of</i> Booze".

496
00:56:22,412 --> 00:56:23,936
A round <i>of</i> applause <i>for</i> him!

497
00:56:25,582 --> 00:56:30,315
Did <i>you know</i> the strongest thing
in the world is booze?

498
00:56:30,453 --> 00:56:33,854
- But it can't knock me down!
- Why not?

499
00:56:33,923 --> 00:56:36,483
Because I always drink lying down!

500
00:56:36,760 --> 00:56:39,854
The strongest thing in the world
is steel!

501
00:56:41,297 --> 00:56:45,461
<i>No!</i> Fire can melt steel!

502
00:56:45,535 --> 00:56:46,866
<i>No,</i> it's not!

503
00:56:48,538 --> 00:56:52,440
Water is stronger,
<i>for</i> it can put out fire!

504
00:56:52,876 --> 00:56:55,436
Ladies and gentlemen,
silence please!

505
00:56:55,512 --> 00:56:57,912
The strongest thing in the world
is the man.

506
00:57:00,316 --> 00:57:03,581
<i>What's stronger than men?</i>

507
00:57:04,220 --> 00:57:06,745
<i>The women!</i>

508
00:57:08,825 --> 00:57:13,285
<i>Yes. The strongest thing</i>
<i>in the world is the woman.</i>

509
00:58:04,714 --> 00:58:05,908
My son.

510
00:58:07,884 --> 00:58:12,878
In this life, we have <i>to do</i>
what we <i>know how to.</i>

511
00:58:15,825 --> 00:58:18,885
Cats drink milk, mice eat cheese...

512
00:58:19,829 --> 00:58:21,558
and I'm a clown.

513
00:58:25,635 --> 00:58:26,863
What about you?

514
01:02:26,909 --> 01:02:28,570
Why did <i>you</i> stop?

515
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:33,279
I'll need that money.

516
01:02:40,423 --> 01:02:41,685
What money?

517
01:03:36,979 --> 01:03:38,412
Lola!

518
01:03:42,451 --> 01:03:43,816
You'll need it.

519
01:05:48,878 --> 01:05:51,244
HELP WANTED

520
01:05:55,217 --> 01:05:58,209
- Are <i>you</i> looking <i>for</i> a clerk?
- Does it say that <i>on</i> the sign?

521
01:05:58,287 --> 01:06:00,278
- Yes.
- Then we are.

522
01:06:00,823 --> 01:06:02,586
And what <i>do</i> I need <i>to</i> apply <i>for</i> it?

523
01:06:02,658 --> 01:06:05,684
An ID, social security
and <i>proof of</i> residence.

524
01:06:09,665 --> 01:06:11,189
Next!

525
01:06:18,808 --> 01:06:21,538
- What a wrecked certificate.
- Yeah.

526
01:06:21,677 --> 01:06:24,771
<i>You'll have to go back and</i>
<i>get a copy at your hometown.</i>

527
01:06:24,847 --> 01:06:26,280
<i>Go</i> back there?

528
01:06:27,583 --> 01:06:28,709
Just kidding!

529
01:06:28,784 --> 01:06:31,412
<i>In two days,</i>
<i>you'll have your ID card.</i>

530
01:06:31,487 --> 01:06:32,784
<i>Next!</i>

531
01:07:11,927 --> 01:07:14,293
- <i>Do you</i> remember me?
- <i>Not</i> really!

532
01:07:16,999 --> 01:07:19,763
Just kidding. Here <i>you go.</i>

533
01:07:23,572 --> 01:07:25,199
<i>Next!</i>

534
01:07:26,442 --> 01:07:29,468
<i>Do you know</i> where
<i>Aldo Auto</i> Parts is at?

535
01:08:04,313 --> 01:08:06,747
ALDO'S AUTO PARTS

536
01:08:27,236 --> 01:08:29,227
<i>How much is 7 times 8?</i>

537
01:08:29,505 --> 01:08:30,665
56?

538
01:08:30,739 --> 01:08:33,469
<i>- Isn't it 58?</i>
- Didn't <i>you</i> ask 7 times 8?

539
01:08:33,542 --> 01:08:35,203
<i>- Right.</i>
- It's 56.

540
01:08:42,485 --> 01:08:43,850
May I help you?

541
01:08:44,320 --> 01:08:47,517
- Is this <i>Aldo Auto</i> Parts?
- Yeah. I'm <i>Aldo.</i>

542
01:08:48,757 --> 01:08:51,351
Oh, <i>so</i> you're <i>Aldo,</i>
like <i>Aldo Auto</i> Parts.

543
01:08:51,560 --> 01:08:52,754
Right.

544
01:08:52,828 --> 01:08:54,386
I'm Benjamim.

545
01:09:00,669 --> 01:09:01,761
<i>Do you</i> need anything?

546
01:09:01,837 --> 01:09:04,635
I'm looking <i>for</i> a lady called Ana.
Does she work here?

547
01:09:04,707 --> 01:09:05,731
Yes, she does.

548
01:09:05,841 --> 01:09:07,536
<i>Honey, come here!</i>

549
01:09:08,344 --> 01:09:09,572
Hi, Ana!

550
01:09:09,645 --> 01:09:12,239
What a surprise!
Is the circus here?

551
01:09:12,314 --> 01:09:13,338
<i>No.</i>

552
01:09:13,415 --> 01:09:15,246
- Have <i>you</i> met <i>Aldo</i> yet?
- Yeah.

553
01:09:15,317 --> 01:09:16,579
What a coincidence!

554
01:09:16,652 --> 01:09:19,883
We're getting married next week.
If <i>you go,</i> it'd be great!

555
01:09:22,291 --> 01:09:23,656
<i>Cool.</i>

556
01:09:29,698 --> 01:09:31,188
Isn't it?

557
01:09:32,001 --> 01:09:33,559
Yeah.

558
01:09:35,704 --> 01:09:38,229
Ok, then!
I'll see you, Ana!

559
01:09:39,308 --> 01:09:40,935
Can I pay <i>for</i> that TV
in installments?

560
01:09:41,010 --> 01:09:44,878
I'll need <i>you</i> ID, social security
and <i>proof of</i> residence.

561
01:10:00,429 --> 01:10:03,557
<i>A guy went to a fortune teller...</i>

562
01:10:03,632 --> 01:10:06,430
<i>and she told him:</i>

563
01:10:06,502 --> 01:10:09,767
<i>"Your mother-in-law</i>
<i>will die a violent death!"</i>

564
01:10:09,838 --> 01:10:12,864
<i>Then he asked:</i>
<i>"Will I be saved?"</i>

565
01:10:15,945 --> 01:10:18,209
<i>Two friends meet.</i>
<i>One of them says:</i>

566
01:10:18,280 --> 01:10:21,545
<i>"I think my wife is seeing</i>
<i>a jockey behind my back."</i>

567
01:10:21,617 --> 01:10:22,675
<i>"Ajockey?"</i>

568
01:10:22,751 --> 01:10:25,379
"Yeah, I found a horse
under the bed."

569
01:10:29,992 --> 01:10:31,584
<i>There's one more.</i>

570
01:10:31,660 --> 01:10:35,391
A Brazilian, a Frenchman
and an Italian...

571
01:10:35,531 --> 01:10:37,396
were sentenced <i>to</i> death.

572
01:10:37,466 --> 01:10:40,196
The executioners asked the Italian:

573
01:10:40,269 --> 01:10:43,705
"What's your last wish?"

574
01:10:43,772 --> 01:10:45,967
<i>"Eating a pizza", he said.</i>

575
01:10:46,542 --> 01:10:48,237
<i>He ate...</i>

576
01:10:49,645 --> 01:10:52,478
and... dropped dead.

577
01:10:52,848 --> 01:10:56,306
Then, <i>to</i> the French one:
"What's your last wish?"

578
01:10:56,452 --> 01:10:58,943
"I'd like a filet mignon."

579
01:10:59,755 --> 01:11:01,518
They gave him...

580
01:11:03,859 --> 01:11:06,623
<i>and he died right away.</i>

581
01:11:06,695 --> 01:11:08,720
<i>Then, they asked the Brazilian guy:</i>

582
01:11:08,797 --> 01:11:11,698
"What <i>do you</i> want
<i>to</i> eat before <i>you</i> die?"

583
01:11:11,767 --> 01:11:12,859
"Strawberries."

584
01:11:12,935 --> 01:11:15,961
"This is <i>not</i> the <i>season</i> yet."
"Fine, I'll wait."

585
01:13:25,367 --> 01:13:28,700
<i>You</i> wretch, this is your son!

586
01:13:28,837 --> 01:13:30,600
What son, madam?

587
01:13:31,573 --> 01:13:33,768
Daddy!

588
01:13:39,715 --> 01:13:43,651
Daddy? Only elephants
have children that big.

589
01:13:44,920 --> 01:13:47,320
What's your name, <i>you</i> silly boy?

590
01:13:47,790 --> 01:13:49,655
Mongrel, sir.

591
01:13:51,293 --> 01:13:53,352
Mongrel?

592
01:13:55,964 --> 01:13:59,365
What're <i>you</i> doing here, Mongrel?

593
01:13:59,935 --> 01:14:01,630
What am I doing here?

594
01:14:01,703 --> 01:14:04,501
Wait, what am I doing?

595
01:14:06,742 --> 01:14:07,936
Oh, I remember!

596
01:14:08,010 --> 01:14:11,241
Cats drink milk, mice eat cheese...

597
01:14:11,313 --> 01:14:12,541
and I'm a clown.

598
01:14:30,766 --> 01:14:31,858
- <i>How</i> are you?
- I'm fine.

599
01:14:31,934 --> 01:14:35,700
I'm talking <i>to</i> the beautiful
lady sitting next <i>to</i> you.

600
01:14:35,838 --> 01:14:37,362
- Is everything fine?
- Yes.

601
01:14:37,439 --> 01:14:39,930
- What's your name, gallant lady?
- It's Wanda.

602
01:14:40,008 --> 01:14:42,533
Is that a <i>good</i> name
<i>to</i> introduce oneself?

603
01:14:43,011 --> 01:14:44,945
<i>Now</i> don't tell me
you're the wife <i>of</i> the...

604
01:14:45,214 --> 01:14:48,650
greatest <i>mayor of</i> South America
and South Lavras?

605
01:14:49,718 --> 01:14:52,516
I bet <i>you</i> don't <i>know</i>
<i>who</i> created nature!

606
01:14:52,588 --> 01:14:53,680
I bet I don't <i>know too!</i>

607
01:14:53,755 --> 01:14:56,246
The world was created by God!

608
01:14:56,592 --> 01:15:00,460
He came over with
His celestial wings...

609
01:15:00,829 --> 01:15:02,592
and <i>took</i> a rib off Adam's body.

610
01:15:02,664 --> 01:15:05,724
- What if a <i>dog</i> walked by?
- <i>God</i> flew away before that.

611
01:15:07,703 --> 01:15:10,228
Then, with that one rib,
He made the first woman.

612
01:15:10,606 --> 01:15:13,939
<i>You know how</i> He named
the woman made <i>from</i> the rib?

613
01:15:14,009 --> 01:15:16,910
- Ribbon?
- Eve, stupid!

614
01:15:17,412 --> 01:15:20,279
Then <i>God</i> made the first couple.

615
01:15:20,883 --> 01:15:23,647
And they had <i>two</i> children,
Cain and Abel.

616
01:15:23,719 --> 01:15:25,516
<i>Who</i> are their parents?

617
01:15:25,587 --> 01:15:27,214
I don't know.
I wasn't there.

618
01:15:27,289 --> 01:15:29,689
<i>So</i> I'd rather <i>not</i> mess with
<i>other families' business.

619
01:15:29,758 --> 01:15:32,659
Your ignorance enrages me.

620
01:15:33,295 --> 01:15:35,229
<i>I'll ask someone from the audience.</i>

621
01:15:35,297 --> 01:15:37,322
- What is your name, sir?
- Jurandir!

622
01:15:37,466 --> 01:15:39,559
Seu Jurandir, are <i>you</i> married?

623
01:15:39,635 --> 01:15:40,932
Yes, I am. This is my wife.

624
01:15:41,003 --> 01:15:43,471
Congratulations!
<i>How</i> many children have <i>you</i> got?

625
01:15:43,539 --> 01:15:44,904
Five children.

626
01:15:45,307 --> 01:15:46,774
Mongrel, that's Jurandir...

627
01:15:46,842 --> 01:15:49,242
<i>who</i> brought five
children <i>into</i> this world!

628
01:15:49,311 --> 01:15:51,609
<i>Who's their father?</i>

629
01:15:51,680 --> 01:15:55,707
I'd rather <i>not</i> get involved
in his familiar issues.

630
01:15:55,984 --> 01:15:58,885
If Jurandir and his wife
brought those five children...

631
01:15:59,521 --> 01:16:01,819
then their father is...

632
01:16:02,691 --> 01:16:04,386
Seu Jurandir!

633
01:16:04,459 --> 01:16:05,790
<i>Now</i> I've <i>got</i> it!

634
01:16:05,928 --> 01:16:08,260
Then I'll ask <i>you</i> something else.

635
01:16:08,330 --> 01:16:10,355
Adam and Eve had <i>two</i> children.

636
01:16:10,566 --> 01:16:12,431
Who's their father?

637
01:16:13,502 --> 01:16:14,628
Seu Jurandir!

638
01:16:14,703 --> 01:16:17,228
Mongrel, that <i>dog</i>
we <i>got</i> back home...

639
01:16:17,306 --> 01:16:20,707
gave birth <i>to</i> seven puppies
last week, didn't she?

640
01:16:21,677 --> 01:16:24,805
Who's the father <i>to</i> those puppies?

641
01:16:24,880 --> 01:16:26,575
Is it Seu Jurandir?

642
01:16:34,389 --> 01:16:35,788
What a beautiful audience!

643
01:16:35,958 --> 01:16:38,654
Turn the lights <i>on</i>
<i>so</i> I can see them!

644
01:16:40,228 --> 01:16:41,855
Turn them off!
Turn them off!

645
01:16:43,932 --> 01:16:47,231
I <i>know</i> it's difficult <i>for</i> someone
<i>who</i> is afraid <i>of</i> roaches...

646
01:16:47,603 --> 01:16:51,198
but I need a brave woman
<i>from</i> the audience!

647
01:16:52,341 --> 01:16:53,968
Nobody?

648
01:16:54,509 --> 01:16:55,669
Then we must call...

649
01:16:55,744 --> 01:16:59,202
the only true brave lady <i>to</i> have
ever set a <i>foot</i> here and there!

650
01:16:59,581 --> 01:17:01,344
- <i>No, no, no!</i>
- Yes, yes, yes!

651
01:17:01,416 --> 01:17:03,247
- <i>No, no, no!</i>
- Yes, yes, yes!

652
01:17:03,318 --> 01:17:04,808
Are <i>you</i> calling?

653
01:17:04,886 --> 01:17:07,184
Exactly! Excuse me, please!

654
01:17:07,422 --> 01:17:08,719
<i>Hello, operator!</i>

655
01:17:08,790 --> 01:17:12,783
<i>I wish to make a collect call to 666,</i>
<i>half a dozen and six.</i>

656
01:17:12,861 --> 01:17:16,422
<i>- That number doesn't exist, madam.</i>
- What?

657
01:17:16,498 --> 01:17:21,197
Hold <i>on</i> while I put <i>you</i> through.

658
01:17:22,738 --> 01:17:25,866
<i>Hello!</i> Is it you, darling?

659
01:17:26,942 --> 01:17:32,471
Could <i>you</i> help us in a <i>mission</i>
<i>of the greatest importance?

660
01:17:32,614 --> 01:17:34,377
<i>How</i> long will <i>you</i> take <i>to</i> get here?

661
